  {
    "key": "01_SHARED_CORE",
    "id": "30fc47c61e218135917bc794bc07b410",
    "title": "01_SHARED_CORE",
    "sample_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "The Self-Build Mechanism"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Every layer exposes self-build interfaces. Users configure, extend, and publish. Growth is driven by user-generated structure, not only content."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "The Validation Workbench"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Nothing becomes truth without validation. Literature, audio, and video are authenticated, indexed, and source-tagged."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Wheels and Knobs Interface Pattern"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Wheel is the state map. Rings are knowledge domains. Knobs are input parameters before, during, and after sessions. Ring and knob changes are linked."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Shared Infrastructure vs Private Silos"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Shared mode supports network effects and low-cost access. Private mode supports isolation and premium compliance needs. Portability remains available."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Regenerative Economics"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Value flow supports creators and project sustainability. Multi-token design is shared across projects rather than fragmented per product."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "Non-Profit Governance Interlock"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "For-profit delivery and non-profit public-good funding are structurally linked but separated to avoid governance capture."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading_2",
        "text": "ISU Tie-In"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "ISU page link: https://www.notion.so/Sustainable-Utilities-Institute-Token-ISU-1b6c47c61e21802e8e3cd167e5c1214e"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "ISU is treated as a practical shared-core example of blockchain-backed agreements, sector token coordination, and transparent funding flows."
      }
    ]
  },
